# 1. Documentation lives in Git as Markdown

Status: accepted

## Context

Documentation kept in wikis drifts from the systems it describes, because changing it is a separate step from changing the system and nobody reviews it.

## Decision

Documentation is Markdown in this repository. Changes go through pull requests and are published automatically on merge.

## Consequences

- A change to a system and the change to its documentation can be reviewed together.
- Broken links fail the build.
- Contributors need Git access, which is a higher bar than a wiki edit button.
